Description: systemE system and service manager
 systemE is a fork of systemd with a reduced set of components and every
 external interface kept identical, so it replaces systemd on an existing
 system without the rest of the system noticing.
 .
 It does not ship systemd-networkd or systemd-resolved: a system that uses
 either needs another network manager and resolver before switching. See
 /usr/share/doc/systeme/README.Debian.

Package: libsysteme0
Architecture: linux-any
Multi-Arch: same
Section: libs
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Provides:
 libsystemd0 (= ${binary:Version}),
 libudev1 (= ${binary:Version}),
Conflicts: libsystemd0, libudev1
Replaces: libsystemd0, libudev1
Description: systemE client libraries
 libsystemd and libudev as built by systemE. The ABI is upstream's,
 unchanged, so packages built against libsystemd0 and libudev1 run against
 these without being rebuilt.

Package: systeme-dev
Architecture: linux-any
Multi-Arch: same
Section: libdevel
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, libsysteme0 (= ${binary:Version})
Provides:
 systemd-dev (= ${binary:Version}),
 libsystemd-dev (= ${binary:Version}),
 libudev-dev (= ${binary:Version}),
Conflicts: systemd-dev, libsystemd-dev, libudev-dev
Replaces: systemd-dev, libsystemd-dev, libudev-dev
Description: systemE development files
 Headers, pkg-config files and the unversioned shared library links for
 libsystemd and libudev.
